Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Topology", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The topology of a substrate is read off its metric balls. The closed balls \
of one radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d127e36b-ca51-4c09-8a22-0c26da8e6d5c"],
 " generate a topology: a vertex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d6a5abff-fb6d-43e2-9dad-3474c97d98a3"],
 " lies in the closure of a vertex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cde8d21f-4694-476a-9f16-619355e4034a"],
 " when the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bab483ef-9d2c-4b8c-8a70-a04af8668ef9"],
 "-ball at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "538dc300-a916-4c85-91ff-92013f28d081"],
 " is contained in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2caa1afd-e56c-4ea2-9a92-9a98a4553009"],
 "-ball at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b23abbc8-ea15-4368-8de9-ba2e41222d6e"],
 ". This specialization preorder carries closure, interior, boundary, \
neighbourhood and continuity. A family of balls forms a complex through its \
intersections: a simplex is admitted when every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e793fd4c-1acb-4990-9247-89cb0113ffe4"],
 " of its balls have a common point, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0bca5b3f-f364-4b00-b207-f8e4226d4197"],
 " gives the Vietoris-Rips complex of twice the radius, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d5f244e-0b97-4e0a-aa26-c19013e055c4"],
 " the Cech complex, and the orders between interpolate. The least number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71f0fb49-3188-4bd0-b4ce-723006348c42"],
 " of balls of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "baf41f58-82b8-415f-b09d-c0cebdd7b7ea"],
 " that cover the substrate falls as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a061251-2ff9-487b-adf6-aa084bb6d7af"],
 " grows, and the rate of that fall is a dimension."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

